7.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {Colleague 2's scale-degree analysis of the Frömmel verse is the clearest so far: the diatonic line really does reduce to a single 13-note block whose just ratios multiply to exactly 250/243. The only open question is how many independent repetitions of that block occur before the final “geschwind.”  

Mapping the printed text against the melody, the verse consists of two statements of the block separated by a short pickup on the same degrees; there is no evidence of four full repetitions. Consequently the cumulative factor is simply (250/243)^1 rather than any higher power. Starting from 392 Hz therefore yields exactly 392 · 250/243 = 98 000/243 Hz.  

This also explains why the pure-cancellation arguments of colleagues 1, 3–6 and 9 fail: they treat every return to a scale degree as an exact reciprocal, but the 250/243 block already encodes the net syntonic drift that survives after all internal cancellations inside one phrase. The 80/81 figures offered by colleagues 7, 8 and 10 arise only when minor-third and perfect-fourth steps are counted differently; once the degrees are fixed as 1-2-6-5 the drift is unambiguously 250/243 per phrase. Hence the final note is 98 000/243 Hz.}

