10.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {Colleagues 1, 2, 3, 6, 8, 9 and 10 have converged on a coherent reading of the Otto–Frömmel verse: the twelve locally just steps leave exactly the syntonic-comma residue 80/81 once the internal 9/8–8/9 and 6/5–5/6 pairs cancel and the truncated tail 1–2–1–6–5–1 is taken into account. The resulting frequency 392 × 80/81 = 31360/81 Hz is therefore the natural pragmatic consensus for a single closed verse.  

Colleague 7’s single 250/243 factor would require an untruncated phrase repetition that the printed text does not contain; the “geschwind” ending simply omits the final return step, removing any justification for that extra drift. At the same time, colleagues 4 and 5’s claim of exact closure rests on treating every scale-degree pair as a perfect reciprocal, which overlooks the path-dependent nature of the local just tuning once the minor-third and perfect-fourth steps are fixed relative to the immediately preceding tone.  

A residual micro-adjustment smaller than 250/243 might still be debated if later analysis shows an extra 81/80 factor hidden in the truncation, but that adjustment would be of second order and would not displace the leading 80/81 result already isolated by the majority. Hence the reduced pair 31360/81 remains the most stable value consistent with both the verse length and the explicit local-just rule.}

